; exit 31 (see .exit)
; MM-LIFE-2h's ARRAY FORM ABOVE THE COUNT FIELD'S CEILING.
;
; `404-container-reference-maps.ax` proves the array form reclaims a
; container's elements. It proves it at cap 8. This one proves it at
; 16,384 words, which is where it used to stop working entirely, and
; the two are separate fixtures because the failure is a CLIFF and not
; a slope: every array-form block from one word to 16,383 was correct,
; and at 16,384 the walk released nothing at all.
;
; WHY. The shape word's count lived in bits 1..14, and `memAlloc`
; clamps a payload past 16,383 words to 0 - the unknown-size sentinel
; `filev` refuses to pool. Release read that same field as the array
; form's LENGTH, so a block past the ceiling said "I am an array of
; zero handles" and the walk stepped over every element it held. The
; count now lives in bits 16..62, written by `Mem.memMarkArray` from
; the ELEMENT count its caller already has, and bits 1..14 stay the
; allocator's size class - the two fields had been asked to be one
; number, and they are not the same number.
;
; MEASURED BEFORE THE FIX (200 iterations of build-a-16,384-element
; reference vector of duplicated strings and free it, peak RSS): the
; `vecNewRef` arm and the `vecNew` arm both measured 335,344 KiB -
; identical to the kilobyte, which is what "the array form is doing
; nothing here" looks like from outside.
;
; EVERY PROBE IS A SHARE COUNT, NOT A FREE-LIST QUERY. `404`'s probes
; ask whether a released block comes back from `memAlloc`, which is the
; right question there and the wrong one here: these vectors grow, and
; a growth allocating out of the same size class the probe is watching
; measures the free list instead of the release. Counting shares asks
; the release path directly - the walk either spent one or it did not -
; and an extra `__retain` keeps the answer readable by making sure the
; probe string never reaches zero and disappears mid-measurement.
;
;   16  the form still works BELOW the cliff: an 8-element reference
;       vector's element loses a share when the vector is freed. This
;       is the control, and it is green on the unfixed compiler -
;       without it a fixture that went red for a build failure would
;       read the same as one that went red for the defect
;    8  THE FIX: a 16,384-element reference vector's element loses a
;       share too
;    4  THE ABLATION, in the fixture: the same 16,384-element program
;       built with `vecNew` does NOT spend it. It passes on the unfixed
;       compiler too - a compiler that reclaims nothing satisfies every
;       "did not release" - which is why it is asserted beside 8 and
;       never alone
;    2  GROWTH ACROSS THE CLIFF DOES NOT DOUBLE-SPEND. `vecPush`
;       doubling 8,192 -> 16,384 marks the abandoned buffer a LEAF
;       before releasing it, because the copy MOVED the shares. Now
;       that the count sits in bits 16..62, `memMarkLeaf` has to clear
;       those bits as well as bit 15: a buffer that kept them would
;       read back as a RECORD WITH A BITMAP, and release would spend a
;       share of whichever payload word the old count happens to name
;       (8,192 = bit 13, so element 13). Every element's count is 1
;       after the growth, and 0 is what the wrong mask produces
;    1  THE ENCODING ITSELF, at the raw layer and independent of
;       `Vec`: a hand-allocated 16,384-word block with bit 15 set and
;       16,384 in bits 16..62 spends the share in word 0. Spelled with
;       `__store64` rather than `memMarkArray` on purpose, so this
;       fixture compiles unchanged against the pre-fix compiler and can
;       be run there
;
; THE UNFIXED COMPILER ANSWERS 22 - 16, 4 and 2, the control and the
; two claims that do not depend on the encoding - and this was RUN, not
; predicted (2026-09-03, against the compiler built from the tree at
; 50ae6a2). Its ABLATION is one line: revert `codegen.ax`'s
; `%pcnt = and i64 %pmap, 140737488355327` in `@axiom_release`'s `popD`
; to the pair of lines that read bits 1..14, rebuild the compiler, and
; this fixture answers 22 again (run, 2026-09-03:
; `FAIL 406-array-form-large-block (exit: expected 31, got 22)`).
;
; AND `404` STAYS GREEN THROUGH THAT ABLATION, which is the reason this
; is a second fixture rather than two more bits in the first one. `404`
; reads the shape words back as literals, and the ablation does not
; change what `memMarkArray` WRITES - only what the release walk reads
; out of it - so `404` had no way to see this and did not.
(import Mem)

(import Str)

(import Vec)

(:: b2i (-> Bool Int))

(fn (b2i x)
  (if x
    1
    0
  )
)

(:: countOf (-> Int Int))

(fn (countOf h) (__load64 (- h 16) 0))

; Push `n` freshly duplicated strings, so the vector crosses every
; growth boundary a real one does.
(:: fillWith (-> (Vec String) Int Int))

(fn (fillWith v n)
  (let ((mut i 0))
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (vecPush v (strDup "abcdefgh"))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      n
    }
  )
)

; Build an `n`-element vector whose first element is a string this
; function keeps an extra share of, free the vector, and answer that
; string's remaining count. `strDup` gives 1, `vecPush` retains to 2,
; the explicit retain makes 3: the walk that reaches the element leaves
; 2 and the walk that does not leaves 3. `refs` picks the constructor
; and is the only difference between probes 8 and 4.
(:: sharesAfterFree (-> Bool Int Int))

(fn (sharesAfterFree refs n)
  (let ((s (strDup "probe")))
    (let ((v 
      (if refs
        vecNewRef
        vecNew
      )
    ))
      {
        (vecPush v s)
        (__retain
          (cast Int s)
        )
        (fillWith v (- n 1))
        (vecFree v)
        (countOf
          (cast Int s)
        )
      }
    )
  )
)

; The smallest share count over elements 0..n-1, read while the vector
; is still live. Recursive rather than a `while` so nothing has to be
; `mut` across the read.
(:: minCount (-> (Vec String) Int Int Int))

(fn (minCount v n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (let ((c 
      (countOf
        (cast Int (vecGet v (- n 1)))
      )
    ))
      (minCount
        v        (- n 1)        (if (< c acc)
          c
          acc
        )
      )
    )
  )
)

; Probe 1, at the raw layer. `nwords` words, array form, count written
; where the fix puts it. Word 0 holds a string's handle and the block
; holds a share of it; the question is whether releasing the block
; spends that share.
(:: rawArrayShares (-> Int Int))

(fn (rawArrayShares nwords)
  (let (
    (s (strDup "raw"))
    (blk (memAlloc (* nwords 8)))
  )
    {
      (__retain blk)
      (memSetWord
        blk        0        (cast Int s)
      )
      (__retain
        (cast Int s)
      )
      (__store64 (- blk 8) 0 (| (| (__load64 (- blk 8) 0) 32768) (* nwords 65536)))
      (__release blk)
      (countOf
        (cast Int s)
      )
    }
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((mut acc 0))
    {
      (set acc (+ acc (* 16 (b2i (== (sharesAfterFree true 8) 2)))))
      (set acc (+ acc (* 8 (b2i (== (sharesAfterFree true 16384) 2)))))
      (set acc (+ acc (* 4 (b2i (== (sharesAfterFree false 16384) 3)))))
      (let ((g vecNewRef))
        {
          (fillWith g 16384)
          (set acc (+ acc (* 2 (b2i (== (minCount g 16384 999) 1)))))
          (vecFree g)
        }
      )
      (set acc (+ acc (b2i (== (rawArrayShares 16384) 1))))
      acc
    }
  )
)
